  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID&apos;s Sustainable Water &amp; Sanitation Systems Activity, North and South Kivu (SWASSA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Democratic Republic of the Congo):  USAID&apos;s Sustainable Water &amp; Sanitation Systems Activity (SWASSA) aims to create sustainable and equitable access to a clean water supply and safe sanitation services through developing the market sector in the Kivus region. Originally, USAID SWASSA envisioned limited infrastructure investment to support performance-based water system management, but after the volcanic eruption in 2021, it increased infrastructure investments to accommodate multi-donor water infrastructure support activities..With FY 2022 funds, USAID SWASSA will provide critical water supply to residents in the peri-urban area of Goma by delivering a large water storage upgrade project, designing and constructing a pumping station. The activity will also support targeted training. USAID SWASSA will promote climate change adaptation measures by increasing the energy efficiency of electromechanical equipment to reduce operators&apos; running costs, establishing bypasses in reservoir systems in case of earthquake damage, creating systems redundancies to avoid service interruption resulting from potential lava flow damage, and diversifying power supply sources..This activity will contribute to Mission Objective 4.1 (Strengthen institutional and community capacity to prevent outbreaks from becoming pandemics as well as respond to and overcome frequent public health and humanitarian emergencies) by supporting sustainable water and sanitation systems. Clean water and sanitation prevents many infectious diseases from spreading and promotes healthier, more stable, and productive communities, thereby reducing threats to U.S. national security. This activity also supports the U.S. Global Water Strategy, the USAID Water and Sanitation Development Plan, and the USAID Climate Strategy...</narrative>
  </description>
